paraphrased_solution:
Note that to go from A=(0,0) to B=(4,3) using only moves of length one along grid edges, one needs exactly four horizontal (eastward) steps and three vertical (northward) steps. Every allowable route is just a sequence of these 7 moves. Hence the total count is the number of ways to choose which 3 of the 7 moves are north; equivalently,
\[
\binom{7}{3}
=\frac{7\cdot6\cdot5}{3\cdot2\cdot1}
=35.
\]

