paraphrased_solution:
1. Total possible unordered pairs of two different numbers from {1,2,3,4,5,6} is C(6,2)=15.  
2. Identify the pairs whose GCD exceeds 1 (i.e., not coprime): 
   • {2,4}  
   • {2,6}  
   • {3,6}  
   • {4,6}  
   There are 4 such “bad” pairs.  
3. Hence the number of coprime selections is 15−4=11.  
4. Therefore, the probability that a randomly chosen pair is relatively prime is 11/15.

